# Snowflake querying

- Read-only outside `SNOWFLAKE_SANDBOX_SCHEMA`. If a task seems to need a write elsewhere, stop and ask.
- Start with metadata, not data: `SHOW DATABASES/SCHEMAS`, `INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES`,
  `INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS` (with ROW_COUNT, BYTES, LAST_ALTERED).
- Search metadata by keyword with `ILIKE` across table names, column names and comments.
- Profile tables with aggregates first: row count, min/max date, distinct keys, null rates.
- Sample with `LIMIT 20` or `SAMPLE (1000 ROWS)`. Never `SELECT *` without LIMIT on tables over ~1M rows.
- Always filter large time-series tables by date when exploring.
- Tag sessions: `ALTER SESSION SET QUERY_TAG = 'freight-agent:<task>'`.
- Save every useful discovery query under `sql/discovery/` with a one-line comment saying what it found.
- Record verified facts (grain, keys, units, coverage, refresh time) in `docs/04_data_catalog.md`.
